CapabilitiesRegistryProposer
├── constructor
│   ├── given a nonzero owner
│   │   └── stores the owner and starts without initialized or proposed capabilities
│   └── given the zero owner
│       └── reverts
├── initCapability
│   ├── when the caller is not the owner
│   │   └── reverts without configuring selectors
│   ├── when the implementation has no code or the selectors are empty
│   │   └── reverts without initializing the implementation
│   ├── when any selector is zero or duplicates an earlier selector
│   │   └── reverts atomically and permits a later valid initialization
│   ├── given a deployed implementation with distinct nonzero selectors
│   │   ├── stores the exact selector order and emits the initialization event
│   │   ├── commits the deployed runtime code hash permanently
│   │   └── does not propose the implementation for any adapter
│   └── given an initialized implementation
│       ├── rejects both identical and replacement selector lists
│       └── remains immutable after revocation or ownership transfer
├── setProposedStatus
│   ├── when the caller is not the owner
│   │   └── rejects both approval and revocation without changing state
│   ├── when approving an uninitialized implementation
│   │   └── reverts without granting permission
│   ├── when revoking an uninitialized implementation
│   │   └── accepts any adapter and implementation address, including zero
│   └── given an initialized implementation
│       ├── grants and revokes only the exact registry, adapter, and implementation tuple
│       ├── rejects changed code or a registry without deployed code when proposing
│       ├── permits withdrawal even when registry or implementation code is absent
│       ├── emits the requested status even when unchanged
│       └── preserves selectors through revocation and reapproval
├── ownership transfer
│   ├── revokes the previous owner's configuration authority
│   └── permits the new owner to initialize and manage approvals
└── getCapabilitySelectors
    ├── returns an empty list for an unknown implementation
    └── returns an independent copy of the immutable configured list
